# What never enters a Docker build context from this repo.
#
# THE SECRETS ARE THE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS (review of #454).
#
# `packages/team/Dockerfile`'s runtime stage does
# `COPY packages/team/deploy packages/team/deploy`, and the runbook's own order
# is `./init.sh` THEN `docker compose build` — so by the time the context is
# assembled, `init.sh` has already written `deploy/.env` holding
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD, RZ_TEAM_DATABASE_URL and RZ_TEAM_INGEST_KEY. With no
# `.dockerignore` anywhere in the tree that file was copied into an image layer,
# where it outlives the rotation recipe in `docs/team-server-runbook.md`
# ("Rotating the ingest key" re-runs init.sh and RESTARTS the app — a restart
# does not rebuild, so the image keeps the old secrets).
#
# This is the sibling of the `.gitignore` finding verify pass 1 caught on #433:
# the atomic write's temp file got an ignore rule and the build context did not.
# Same file, same 348 bytes, one boundary out.
packages/team/deploy/.env
packages/team/deploy/.env.tmp.*

# Nothing below is a secret — it is context the daemon never needs. No stage of
# any Dockerfile here copies either: `packages/team/Dockerfile` installs its own
# `node_modules` with `npm ci` in the deps stage, and nothing reads `.git`.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
